# The images consume the generated tree (`build/`) plus `docker/selfcheck.py`,
# and nothing else here. These are the entries big enough to matter: the
# upstream clone alone is ~514 MB, several times the image it is not part of.
#
# Deny-list rather than `*` + negations: re-including a nested path under a
# blanket `*` depends on directory-traversal subtleties that are easy to get
# subtly wrong, and the win would be a few hundred KB.
upstream-geoips/
.upstream-cache.git/

.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.log
*.json
